---
/*
 * The running stitch (ponto corrido): the logo's thread going in and out of the
 * paper. It is the publication's only divider (DESIGN.md), used where one
 * section is sewn onto the next. An SVG line instead of a CSS gradient, so
 * each stitch gets round ends like real thread; x2="100%" stretches it to
 * any width without distorting the stitches.
 */
---

<svg class="stitch" height="6" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
  <line x1="1.5" y1="3" x2="100%" y2="3"></line>
</svg>

<style>
  .stitch {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 6px;
    /* The round cap of the last stitch may pass the right edge by 1px. */
    overflow: visible;
    color: var(--color-thread);
  }
  /* Round caps add half the stroke at each end: 9 + 2.25 ≈ 11px of visible
     thread, 8 - 2.25 ≈ 6px of paper between stitches. */
  line {
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 2.25;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-dasharray: 9 8;
  }
</style>
